        "target": "Given:\n- Matt climbs at 6 feet/minute.\n- Jason climbs at 12 feet/minute.\n- Time climbed: 7 minutes.\n\nTo find how much higher Jason will be than Matt after 7 minutes, we calculate the distance each has climbed and then find the difference.\n\nMatt's height after 7 minutes:\n\\[ 6 \\, \\text{feet/minute} \\times 7 \\, \\text{minutes} = 42 \\, \\text{feet} \\]\n\nJason's height after 7 minutes:\n\\[ 12 \\, \\text{feet/minute} \\times 7 \\, \\text{minutes} = 84 \\, \\text{feet} \\]\n\nThe difference in height:\n\\[ 84 \\, \\text{feet} - 42 \\, \\text{feet} = 42 \\, \\text{feet} \\]\n\nSo, Jason will be 42 feet higher than Matt after 7 minutes.\n\nFINAL: 42",
